        "review_4": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "1",
            "before": "Tried every trap and poison for 3 years solid. Nothing lasted more than a week.",
            "headline": "Finally, something that keeps them gone — for good.",
            "body": "<p>Put pouches under the kitchen sink and along the cellar wall. Eleven days later, not one mouse. Six weeks on — still nothing. My wife actually feels at ease in her own kitchen again. I honestly wish I'd found this years ago.</p>",
            "name": "Robert L.",
            "location": "🏠 Homeowner · Shropshire",
            "purchased": "2 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-01.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_5": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "1",
            "before": "Spent nearly £150 on traps, poison and one of those plug-in ultrasonic things. Nothing worked more than a few days.",
            "headline": "I wasted £150+ on traps, then I found Old Tom's...",
            "body": "<p>Pouches behind the fridge, along the garage wall, under the floorboards. By week two — total silence. I was ready to ring pest control and spend £300. Glad I didn't.</p>",
            "name": "Tom W.",
            "location": "🏠 Homeowner · Leeds, West Yorkshire",
            "purchased": "3 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-02.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_6": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "1",
            "before": "Old house, loads of gaps. Had mice every single winter for six years. First October in six years I haven't had to deal with them.",
            "headline": "This just works, that's all I want to say!!!",
            "body": "<p>Lined every cellar corner and both garage door edges before the cold set in. Usually by mid-October I'm setting traps every other day. Not this year. Not one.</p>",
            "name": "Amelia R.",
            "location": "🏠 Homeowner · Harrogate, North Yorkshire",
            "purchased": "3 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-03.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_7": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "2",
            "before": "We live in our motorhome full time. Tried every spray and trap going — mice kept coming back whenever we parked up somewhere rural.",
            "headline": "Three months on a farm site in Devon. Not one mouse the whole time.",
            "body": "<p>Put pouches under every seat, in both lockers and the garage compartment. Didn't think something this simple would work. Haven't touched a trap since. For full-timers it's the only thing that's actually worked for us.</p>",
            "name": "Dave B.",
            "location": "🚐 Full-Time Motorhomer · Keswick, Cumbria",
            "purchased": "3 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-04.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_8": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "2",
            "before": "Mice had wrecked my caravan two winters running. Chewed wiring, shredded insulation — thousands in damage.",
            "headline": "Opened her up in spring and not a single mouse. First time in three years.",
            "body": "<p>Tucked pouches in the front locker, by the wheel arches and in every storage space before laying her up for winter. Took her out four months later, completely untouched. First time in three years. Already ordered a second lot for next season.</p>",
            "name": "Gary M.",
            "location": "🚐 Caravan Owner · Skegness, Lincolnshire",
            "purchased": "2 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-05.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_9": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "2",
            "before": "Got my caravan out of storage last April and the damage was shocking. Chewed seat cushions, droppings everywhere.",
            "headline": "This season — spotless. Not a dropping, not a chew mark. Nothing.",
            "body": "<p>Put pouches in all four lockers and two under the dinette before shutting her up. Six months later, opened it up spotless. Saved myself a £500 repair bill at least.</p>",
            "name": "Russell O.",
            "location": "🚐 Caravan Owner · Whitby, North Yorkshire",
            "purchased": "3 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-06.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_10": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "3",
            "before": "Lost so much feed to mice every single year. Tried poison but was always worried about my dogs and cattle getting at it.",
            "headline": "Six weeks in — feed room's clean. Dogs are fine. Haven't touched a trap since.",
            "body": "<p>Put pouches round the whole feed store, every 2.5 metres like the instructions said. Within two weeks the droppings stopped completely. What got me is there's nothing to clear up — no dead mice, no poison, no mess. Just gone.</p>",
            "name": "Dale T.",
            "location": "🌾 Farmer · Hereford, Herefordshire",
            "purchased": "5 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-07.jpg"
          }
        },
        "review_11": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "3",
            "before": "Every autumn without fail — mice moved into the machinery shed and feed room the second it turned cold.",
            "headline": "Set them out in September this year. October came and went. Nothing.",
            "body": "<p>Covered the feed room perimeter and tucked pouches inside three bits of kit that always got hit. Didn't have to set a single trap all season. First clean winter in eight years.</p>",
            "name": "Thomas E.",
            "location": "🌾 Farmer · Malton, North Yorkshire",
            "purchased": "5 Pack",
            "avatar_asset": "oldtoms-testimonial-08.jpg"
          }
